=========================================================
              PROTOTYPE DESIGN PATTERN
=========================================================

CATEGORY:
Creational Design Pattern

INTENT (MOST IMPORTANT):
"Create new objects by copying an existing prototype
instead of constructing from scratch."

Simple one-line:
"Heavy object ko baar-baar new banane ke bajaye clone karo."

Golden line:
Copy existing configured object → tweak → use

---------------------------------------------------------
1) CORE INTUITION
---------------------------------------------------------

Soch game me Alien NPC banana expensive hai:

Constructor work:
- DB se template load
- textures load
- stats calculate
- AI tree initialize
- inventory attach
- weapon setup

Agar 100 aliens chahiye:
100 baar constructor chalana expensive ❌

Better:
1 heavy template banao
baaki sab clone kar lo ✅

This is Prototype.

---------------------------------------------------------
2) PROBLEM IT SOLVES
---------------------------------------------------------

Without prototype:
Repeated heavy object creation

Problems:
1. expensive constructors
2. duplicate setup logic
3. repeated DB/API calls
4. config recreation
5. object graph creation cost

Prototype solves:
"reuse initialized object state"

---------------------------------------------------------
3) WHEN TO USE
---------------------------------------------------------

Use when:
1. object creation expensive ho
2. similar objects baar-baar chahiye
3. partially configured copies chahiye
4. object graph clone karna ho
5. template based instances chahiye

Golden trigger:
"template object se multiple variants"

---------------------------------------------------------
4) UML DIAGRAM
---------------------------------------------------------

                 +----------------------+
                 |      Cloneable       |
                 +----------------------+
                 | +clone()             |
                 +----------------------+
                           ^
                           |
                    +--------------+
                    |     NPC      |
                    +--------------+
                    | name         |
                    | health       |
                    | attack       |
                    | defense      |
                    +--------------+
                    | +clone()     |
                    +--------------+

Client:
Template -> clone -> modify -> use

---------------------------------------------------------
5) PARTICIPANTS
---------------------------------------------------------

1) Prototype Interface
clone() contract define karta

2) Concrete Prototype
Actual clone logic
NPC

3) Client
Existing object clone karta

---------------------------------------------------------
6) WHY WE NEED IT
---------------------------------------------------------

Need because:
- constructor costly
- setup repeated
- object graph large
- templates reusable
- variants quickly chahiye

Most important:
"construction cost ko copy cost me convert karna"

---------------------------------------------------------
7) REAL LIFE EXAMPLES
---------------------------------------------------------

1. Game NPC templates
2. Resume template cloning
3. Document duplicate
4. Slide duplicate in PPT
5. Workflow draft copy
6. Form template reuse
7. VM snapshot clone
8. Kubernetes pod template

---------------------------------------------------------
8) PROTOTYPE vs STRATEGY (VERY IMPORTANT 🔥)
---------------------------------------------------------

Prototype aur Strategy completely different intents.

---------------------------------------------------------
PROTOTYPE:
---------------------------------------------------------
Intent:
Object creation by cloning

Focus:
Creation optimization

Problem:
Heavy object creation

Example:
NPC clone
Document duplicate

---------------------------------------------------------
STRATEGY:
---------------------------------------------------------
Intent:
Swap algorithm/behavior

Focus:
Behavior variation

Problem:
Different algorithms

Example:
Sort strategy
Payment method

---------------------------------------------------------
KEY DIFFERENCE:
---------------------------------------------------------

Prototype:
"new object kaise banega"

Strategy:
"behavior kaise chalega"

---------------------------------------------------------
9) SHALLOW vs DEEP COPY (INTERVIEW GOLD)
---------------------------------------------------------

VERY IMPORTANT 🚀

Shallow Copy:
Pointers/references copied only

Deep Copy:
Nested objects bhi clone hote

Example:
NPC has Weapon*
Then weapon bhi clone karna hoga

Interviewers love this follow-up.

---------------------------------------------------------
10) ADVANTAGES
---------------------------------------------------------

1. Fast object creation
2. Reuse expensive setup
3. Cleaner creation logic
4. Runtime cloning
5. Template-based variants
6. Avoid constructor complexity

---------------------------------------------------------
11) DISADVANTAGES
---------------------------------------------------------

1. Deep copy tricky
2. cyclic refs hard
3. clone bugs possible
4. hidden copy cost

---------------------------------------------------------
12) INTERVIEW ANSWER TEMPLATE
---------------------------------------------------------

"Prototype pattern creates new objects by cloning existing
fully or partially configured instances, making object
creation faster and avoiding expensive reconstruction."

---------------------------------------------------------
13) GOLDEN TAKEAWAY
---------------------------------------------------------

Prototype = expensive construction ko cheap cloning me convert karo

